  "about": "How the game picks between two definitions of one object. One row per game folder; a row also covers the folders inside it unless a deeper row says otherwise. Folders with no row use 'default'. 'checked' is the date a live run confirmed the row, empty until then.",
  "units": {
    "key": "Each top-level `name = { ... }` is one object, named by its key",
